{"name":"Cherry Mahogany","hex":"#6a332d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"},{"term":"mahogany","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The valuable wood of any of various tropical American evergreen trees, of the genus Swietenia, mostly used to make furniture. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any of the trees from which such wood comes."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of mahogany.","Having the colour of mahogany; dark reddish-brown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mahogany"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tieghemella heckelii","blocks":[{"text":"Tieghemella heckelii is a tree species of the genus Tieghemella in the plant family Sapotaceae. The species occurs in Cameroon, Ivory Coast, Gabon, Ghana, Liberia, Nigeria, and Sierra Leone and is threatened by habitat loss and over exploitation. This timber tree species can grow up to 45 meters tall and 1.2 meters in diameter. One individual, the Big Tree of Oda, is 66.5 m (218 ft) tall and 396 cm (13 ft) in diameter and is believed to be the tallest tree in West Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Tieghemella_heckelii_3310694.jpg/330px-Tieghemella_heckelii_3310694.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tieghemella_heckelii"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Mahogany","blocks":[{"text":"Mahogany is a straight‑grained, reddish‑brown timber produced by three tropical hardwood species of the genus Swietenia, native to the Americas and belonging to the pantropical chinaberry family, Meliaceae. The term refers specifically to wood from Swietenia macrophylla, Swietenia mahagoni, and Swietenia humilis. Of these, S. macrophylla is the most widespread and the only species widely grown commercially."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Genuine_Mahogany_veneer_with_ripple_marks.jpg/330px-Genuine_Mahogany_veneer_with_ripple_marks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahogany"},{"title":"Cerise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerise is a dark pink shade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bandyball1.jpg/330px-Bandyball1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerise_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/500px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/1280px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG/500px-Italienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prunus avium, sweet cherry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalienische_S%C3%BC%C3%9Fkirschen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w